From d37e111297e70008a982aa821e4cd00c45f8f0b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tsm-consultz <brightmindsfinancial@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 02:32:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: Task Data Requirements Registry for RCM OS
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Closes the gap from the earlier compliance.html/finops-operations.html
audit: the AI Assistant could only give generic guidance because
nothing defined what data a given cadence phase actually needs from
its owning module. This adds that definition and wires it through.

- data/rcm/task-requirements.json: registry keyed by `${cadence}-${phaseIndex}`
  (matches the existing taskKey convention), 12 phase entries across
  Daily/Weekly/Month-End, fields grounded directly in the tasks/purpose
  text already in CADENCES -- nothing invented.
- routes/rcm-requirements.js: GET /api/rcm/requirements (serves the
  registry), GET/POST /api/rcm/self-reported, DELETE .../:key/:fieldId.
  In-memory store, same convention as routes/rcm-relay.js.
- tsm-rcm-os.html: each phase card now renders a "Data to gather from
  [module]" block with inputs + save, badged "self-reported · date"
  once filled -- never presented as verified. Executive tab gets a
  matching self-reported summary panel. buildAssistantContext() and
  fetchGuidance()'s request body both include self-reported values,
  explicitly labeled unverified.
- routes/rcm-relay.js: /api/rcm/guidance now accepts selfReported[],
  passes it to the Groq prompt with instructions to phrase it as
  self-reported (never as confirmed/audited), and the heuristic
  fallback surfaces non-empty self-reported findings the same way it
  already does for open exceptions.

Verified end-to-end against a locally running instance of the full
server.js (registry GET, self-reported POST/GET round-trip, guidance
heuristic correctly surfaces a non-zero self-reported value and
filters out a "none" one, page HTML renders the new blocks, assistant
script paths resolve 200).

No real backend data exists yet for compliance.html et al. -- this is
intentionally the self-reporting layer, not a fix for that. The
validation layer (compare self-reported vs. a real value once a
module exposes one) is still a follow-up, not built here.
